(b) THE LOOSE STEP: iterated peel needs V(Bu{f1}); track its growth (adjacent f2=f1+1)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   base B = consec_8,  peel f2=f1+1 first => intermediate base Bu{f1}:
        f1   V(B)  V(Bu_f1)  (6/49)V(Bu_f1)/f2   C=I_B-Phi2
        15     45        63           0.482143    0.0021241
        20     45        67           0.390671    0.0062057
        40     45        93           0.277750    0.0092048
        80     45       163           0.246410    0.0111598
       160     45       296           0.225124    0.0138551
       320     45       546           0.208278    0.0115168

   => V(Bu{f1}) GROWS ~ 7*f1 (the far element fragments every B_j into ~7 arcs each),
      so (6/49)V(Bu{f1})/f2 ~ (6/49)*7*f1 / (f1+1) -> 6/7 = 0.857, a CONSTANT, NOT 0.
      The iterated single-peel bound is therefore LOOSE by O(1): it cannot show the
      curvature -> small.  THIS IS THE PRECISE LOOSE STEP (slope-1 resonance, HYP-2776).

